# Build context exclusions for the Unslothed images.
#
# This file is load-bearing, not hygiene. packaging/dist alone is ~4 GB of
# PyInstaller output and packaging/Output holds a 1.91 GB installer; without
# these lines every `docker build` uploads them to the daemon before running a
# single instruction, on both tags, on every rebuild.

# --- packaging output (the expensive ones) ---
packaging/dist/
packaging/build/
packaging/Output/
packaging/__pycache__/
packaging/unsloth_compiled_cache/

# --- VCS and IDE ---
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
.superpowers/

# --- Python build/runtime droppings ---
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
build/
dist/
*.egg
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
unsloth_compiled_cache/

# --- Node ---
# node_modules is reinstalled by `npm ci` inside the frontend stage; copying the
# host's (Windows, and ~1 GB) would be both wrong and slow.
**/node_modules/
studio/frontend/dist/

# --- Rust / Tauri shell (not part of either image) ---
studio/src-tauri/target/

# --- tests and local scratch ---
**/.DS_Store
*.log
*.tmp
